<AddOnInstructionDefinition Use="Target" Name="MODVLV_AOI" Revision="1.0" ExecutePrescan="false" ExecutePostscan="false" ExecuteEnableInFalse="false" CreatedDate="2026-10-26T16:25:14.629Z" CreatedBy="LEWISBIO-1\TS-Admin" EditedDate="2026-10-30T22:50:00.000Z" EditedBy="LEWISBIO-1\TS-Admin" SoftwareRevision="v38.01"
>
<Description>
<![CDATA[simple modulating valve control.
Note: Use with MODVALVE_PIDE_AOI if you need to control valve position with a PIDE command]]>
</Description>
<RevisionNote>
<![CDATA[rev 1.0: initial creation on 10/26/26
10/30/26: added config_type (0 = analog position feedback, 1 = fully opened / fully closed limit switches), FullyOpened_hwdi, FullyClosed_hwdi and Position_SP (used when config_binary = 0); revision number not changed
10/30/26: config_type 1 FailOpen / FailClose now arm only when the commanded end state is that limit (config_binary 1 commanded open / closed, or config_binary 0 with Position_SP at 100 / 0); Position_SP between 0 and 100 arms neither; Help text updated; revision number not changed
10/30/26: parameter descriptions shortened (config_binary, config_type, Position_SP); config_pos_fullyClosed and config_pos_fullyOpened made Visible; Help text unchanged; revision number not changed]]>
</RevisionNote>
<AdditionalHelpText>
<![CDATA[MODVLV_AOI: valve command, position feedback and alarms

config_binary (BOOL, Visible, not Required)
Config values are set once by hand in the instance data structure, not wired in the call.
1 = the valve is ON/OFF only. The command is only ever 0% or 100%: AutoCall true sends 100, false sends 0.
0 = the valve is modulating. AutoCall true sends Position_SP (limited to 0 to 100%), false sends 0.
Applies to every config_type.

config_type (DINT, Visible, not Required)
0 = analog position feedback. Position_FDBK_hwai and its OverRange_hwdi, UnderRange_hwdi and Fault_hwdi are used. FailOpen and FailClose compare the analog position with config_pos_fullyOpened and config_pos_fullyClosed. FullyOpened_hwdi and FullyClosed_hwdi are not used.
1 = limit-switch feedback, no analog position feedback. FullyOpened_hwdi and FullyClosed_hwdi are used. Position_FDBK_hwai and its range and fault inputs are ignored (wire a literal 0 or a dummy tag). There is no channel-fault alarm. Position_scai shows the command, 100 at the open limit and 0 at the closed limit. State: 0 = open, 1 = closed, 2 = traveling (both limits off), 99 = both limits made.
In type 1 FailOpen and FailClose only arm when that limit is the expected end state, so a valve held between the limits raises neither alarm:
- FailOpen arms when the open limit is not made and the valve is commanded fully open: config_binary 1 with AutoCall true, or config_binary 0 with AutoCall true and Position_SP at 100 (or above, since the command is limited to 100).
- FailClose arms when the closed limit is not made and the valve is commanded fully closed: AutoCall false, or config_binary 0 with AutoCall true and Position_SP at 0 (or below).
- Any Position_SP strictly between 0 and 100 (config_binary 0, AutoCall true) arms neither alarm and clears a pending fail timer. State stays 2 while both limits are off.
Any other config_type value behaves as type 0.
When a new type is added, add it to this list.]]>
</AdditionalHelpText>
